// tests/probes/ship_long.eeai's first leg in a busy game (run with ai_count=3): 120 of P1's macemen on its island march
// between 24,38 and 30,30 every 15 s (each one its own path request, `move`), while the dreadnought sails 60,14 -> 45,70
// traced every step (# fmtrace) - does it wait for its next piece of route when the path requests queue up?
wait_until(0.1min)
spawn(1, unit.s10_dreadnought_battleship, 60, 14, 1)
spawn(1, unit.inf03_maceman, 22, 40, 60)
spawn(1, unit.inf03_maceman, 26, 36, 60)
wait_until(0.3min)
cmd("fmove go 1 60 14 2 45 70")
cmd("fmove trace 0")
every(30s, 0.3min, 3min, (run) => {
    cmd("move 1 24 38 14 30 30")
    wait(15s)
    cmd("move 1 30 30 14 24 38")
})
wait_until(3min)
